  <h2>Understanding Your Military BAH: Home Buying Budget Planning</h2>

  <p>Your Basic Allowance for Housing (BAH) is the foundation of your military home buying budget. Understanding how to use it strategically is key to successful homeownership.</p>

  <h3>What is BAH?</h3>
  <p>BAH is a monthly housing allowance based on your rank, location, and dependent status. It's designed to help offset housing costs for military families.</p>

  <h3>San Antonio BAH Rates</h3>
  <p>San Antonio has different BAH rates depending on your rank. Your BAH directly impacts how much home you can afford.</p>

  <h3>Calculating Your Home Budget</h3>
  <p>A good rule of thumb: your total housing costs (mortgage + taxes + insurance + HOA) should fit comfortably within your BAH, ideally using 70-80% of your allowance.</p>

  <h3>Building Equity</h3>
  <p>Unlike renting, your BAH payment builds home equity. Over your military career, this creates significant wealth through home appreciation and mortgage principal paydown.</p>

  <h2>Maximizing Your BAH Benefit</h2>
  <p>Let's discuss your specific BAH and create a budget that works for your family while building long-term wealth.</p>
